{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Chariots</b> — 4 times in the Masorah: here, and: ואת מרכבות השמש שרף באש, in the account of Josiah when he eradicated idolatry — teaches that Pharaoh and his army would embroider their idolatry on their garments, and: מרכבות כבודך, regarding Shebna who went to make peace with Sennacherib and to worship idolatry. But I do not know myself to be good [enough for] idolatry — rather: מרכבות עמי נדיב, as written: רוכב שמים בעזרך." "<b>And the choice</b> — 2 times: here, and: ומבחר בחוריו ירדו לטבח — that after they drowned in the sea, their limbs descended to be slaughtered on the rocks of the sea."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The phrase אני לא ידעתי נפשי בטוב ע\"א is textually difficult; translated hyper-literally. The abbreviation ע\"א (עבודת אלילים = idolatry) appears to thread through all four occurrences."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:01.291296348Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}